WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.533
Pieces of

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:01.634
the Titan submersible

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.369
that imploded

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:03.870
with five people on board

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.939
have been retrieved from the ocean floor.

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:06.806
It's been more than a week

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:07.607
since the sub's

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.309
ill-fated voyage to the Titanic

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.910
wreck in the North Atlantic.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.213
CNN's Paula Newton is in Ottawa for us.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.648
Paula, tell us more about the pieces

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:16.883
that were brought in today

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:17.484
and what else

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:18.985
officials are looking at

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:22.122
as this investigation continues.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:23.890
Yeah, so those pieces of debris

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:24.190
you see

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.026
beyond are from pelagic research,

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.327
and they're the ones that operated

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.162
the remote operated vehicle

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.897
near the Titanic wreck.

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:31.498
They had first

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:33.400
mapped out the debris field.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.701
And then what's extraordinary

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:35.101
here, Brianna,

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:35.835
is that they brought up

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:38.204
such large pieces of Titan.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.873
You can actually see

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.608
the dome and the viewport.

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:42.308
And if you compare

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:43.510
what they brought up today

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.079
to the submersible one, it was intact.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.214
Certainly a lot to go by there.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.349
We had been told by the U.S.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:49.783
Coast Guard

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:51.885
when they first announced this tragedy

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.353
that in their term,

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:54.988
the area was unforgiving

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.756
in a very challenging and remote area

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.158
in which to recover debris.

00:00:58.158 --> 00:00:59.159
But here we are.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:02.128
We do see quite a few pieces of it.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:03.229
I have to say, obviously,

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.464
as with some disquiet,

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:06.232
this is the resting place

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.067
for five people

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.368
who tragically lost their lives.

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:08.802
And I'm sure

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:09.602
while the family members

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:10.203
are glad to see

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.504
that there will be these clues

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:12.705
in the investigation,

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.507
it's obviously causing

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.842
so much grief again

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.377
to see all of this play out.

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:18.144
I will say, though,

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:18.912
this investigation

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.146
is very important, though,

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.082
to many people and many countries.

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:22.882
Right here in Canada,

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.451
the Transportation Safety Board

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.453
trying to determine exactly what went on.

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:27.954
They've conducted many interviews.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.722
They refused to say to me today

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.192
where those pieces of debris are headed,

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.094
but they will be headed to labs either

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.595
in the United States or Canada

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.330
to be examined further

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.465
And I will mention as well

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:38.932
beyond that,

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.700
obviously, the RCMP,

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.601
the national police force

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.802
here, is determining

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.671
whether or not a criminal investigation

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:45.572
needs to be opened.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.039
And again,

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.674
the more that they can salvage

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:48.508
from the deep sea,

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.009
the more that they will have answers,

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.011
because the last thing anyone wants here

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:54.180
is for this to be a guessing game.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.615
So this recovery and important

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.583
operation beyond

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.517
and I'm sure is

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:58.651
as painful as

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.953
this may be for the family

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.054
of the victims families,

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.789
I'm sure they would like to see

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:03.823
some of this evidence

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:04.557
as well and see where

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.126
this investigation leads

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:07.260
Paula Newton, thank you.

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:10.263
Well, joining us now is Bart Kemper.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:11.131
He's an engineer

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.999
and was one of the dozen experts

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.934
in the submersible craft industry

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.303
who actually raised concerns in 2018

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.471
about how Ocean Gates

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.473
Titan vessel was made.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.508
He warned back then

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:22.242
that the company's

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:23.409
experimental approach

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:24.377
could result

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:26.546
in catastrophic consequences.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:27.847
And of course, we did

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:30.016
see that exact thing play out.

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:30.717
Bart,

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:31.751
what do you make

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.786
of the size of the pieces

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.823
that have been recovered thus far?

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.993
This is consistent with an implosion.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:42.195
Don't forget, an implosion is.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:44.264
It collapses in on itself.

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:46.032
It's not an explosion.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.301
So the have the living quarters,

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.469
which is the only part

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.037
that's supposed to be at one atmosphere

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.005
or the normal

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.806
what we breathe atmosphere,

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:55.909
it will collapse inwards on that.

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:58.077
But the rest of the items are

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:58.811
what we call it in

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.480
potable volumes or volumes

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.514
that that are not part

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:02.382
of the living space,

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:04.250
which would be the batteries,

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.719
lights, the gas cylinders.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.221
Those aren't part of the

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:10.089
the one atmosphere place

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:12.125
where the where the crew would be

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.259
so that

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.427
those would still be intact,

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:15.795
as would be the framework

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:17.463
that's holding it all together.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:20.099
So I'm not surprised to see large pieces

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.167
come out.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.268
It's just a question of

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.603
which pieces are coming up.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:24.637
And of course,

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.940
what the investigation leads us to.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.007
So if you were doing reverse

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:28.975
engineering here,

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.677
as we're seeing and learning

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.745
more about these pieces,

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.180
what are some of the questions

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.281
that you'll be asking

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.819
I would want to know the

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:42.789
thickness and composition of the carbon

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:44.157
fiber composite.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:45.858
It's not just a question of the thickness

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:47.660
because it's not one solid

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.962
piece of carbon fiber.

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:49.963
It's a composite

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:52.198
or multiple layers of different materials

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.132
and different

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.267
different orientations

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:54.901
that would give it

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.669
its strength in compression

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:57.904
The reason why I say compression

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:58.771
is because

00:03:58.771 --> 00:03:59.906
it's an external pressure,

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.074
so it's pushing in on it.

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:02.442
If it was

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.877
a internal pressure like a

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:07.714
like a medical hyperbaric chamber,

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:10.283
if you pull it outwards.

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:11.251
The other thing

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:12.585
I similarly would want to link

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.988
the dimensions of the window,

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:16.856
which is made of acrylic

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.124
as well as the dimensions

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:20.460
and thickness of the titanium cap.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.395
Another critical part be

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.897
how everything comes together because

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:25.832
we're the joints coming

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.033
together will be a

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.568
potential point of failure.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:29.702
So you'd want to

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.271
have a good examination of that.

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.772
So hopefully

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:33.806
some of these components

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:34.507
are still connected

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:35.975
the way they're supposed to be.

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:37.143
So the investigators

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:39.512
will be able to properly assess

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:41.281
what was the failure modes

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:43.483
and what was the actual cause

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:46.185
of the collapse I know you had warned

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.488
Ocean Gate to comply

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:49.589
with some of the U.S.

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:51.424
regulations for this industry.

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:53.092
What kind of changes

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:54.160
or safety features

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:55.395
need to be made

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:57.163
so so that this doesn't happen again?

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.064
Or is this as simple

00:04:58.064 --> 00:04:59.832
as perhaps complying with U.S.

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.734
regulation could have

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.069
avoided this from happening?

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:05.938
Well,

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:07.173
more to the point with this,

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:08.941
this is out of international waters.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:09.609
So this B

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:10.543
I am o were

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:12.845
the International Marine Organization.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.113
That's where the rules would be.

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.381
However,

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:16.849
you are correct

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:19.052
that this was an experimental

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:21.154
not a tourist sub, not a researcher,

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:23.823
but a very much an experimental item

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.625
that has not been built

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:26.993
to an existing codes

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:27.593
and standard

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:28.861
such as pressure

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:30.663
vessels for human occupancy

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.198
published in United States

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.500
or any of the classification societies

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.270
such as American Bureau, Shipping or DMV.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:38.705
Those are

00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:40.440
that's how these other submarines

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:40.907
are done.

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:43.343
And it's as has been mentioned before.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.611
There are nine or ten other submarines,

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.080
non-governmental ones,

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.348
that can reach this depth

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:50.883
and not had a problem.

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:51.818
All right, Bert Kemper,

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:52.852
thank you so much.

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:53.853
We appreciate your time.

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:55.888
Thank you.

